  "identifier": "mimic-iv",
  "name": "MIMIC-IV",
  "alternateName": [
    "Medical Information Mart for Intensive Care IV"
  ],
  "description": "Large de-identified EHR dataset from 364,627 patients across 546,028 hospital admissions and 94,458 ICU stays at Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center (BIDMC), Boston. Organised into two modules: hosp (hospital-wide EHR: admissions, diagnoses, procedures, labs, prescriptions, microbiology) and icu (ICU clinical information system: charted events, inputs/outputs, procedures, datetimes). Time period 2008–2022, de-identified to 2100–2200 range. v3.1 (October 2024). Linked datasets include MIMIC-IV-Note (clinical notes), MIMIC-IV-ED (emergency department), and MIMIC-CXR (chest X-rays). PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data License 1.5.0 — requires free PhysioNet credentialing, CITI training completion, and DUA signature. The most widely used open clinical EHR dataset for ICU prediction, clinical NLP, and foundation model development.",
  "url": "https://physionet.org/content/mimiciv/",
  "license": "PhysioNet-CHDL-1.5",
  "version": "3.1",
  "dateModified": "2024-10-11",
